WEBVTT

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.750
You came all this way in the snow.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.210
But both my sister Gio and
Hotoke-Gozen are no longer...

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.510
I know.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:32.180
For a time, we were able
to live tranquil lives together.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.060
Come to think of it,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:40.600
a <i>shirabyoshi </i>who visited my sister
here mentioned something.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.190
She said she met a woman
with the same eye color as you.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.320
She said the woman was once a <i>shirabyoshi</i>.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.400
Where is she now?

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.780
Let's send a letter to the <i>shirabyoshi</i>
who visited and ask.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:13.210
THE HEIKE STORY

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.380
Episode 8

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.680
You mustn't eat that, my emperor.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.180
Let 's give that back
to Lord Atsumori now.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.020
Sorry.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.110
So then Biwa didn't come to stay
with you either, Lady Tokuko?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.700
No.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.580
I would have liked to see her.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:06.920
But... it may be best for her not
to be involved with us anymore.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.310
This is a cat?

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.850
It's so cute!

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.060
Thank you.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.270
You're welcome, dear.
Sorry we only have such thin soup.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.280
Where are you headed?

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.400
A place called Echigo.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.700
Echigo?

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:40.410
I am told it is many
mountains away from here.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.490
My goodness.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.660
Why are you going so far?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.790
That's probably where my Ma is.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:53.880
Be careful, dear. Fleeing Genji
warriors may be lurking about.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:04:00.340
Nearby in Sunomatagawa, there was
a battle between the Genji and the Heike.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.100
We lost.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.850
Have some backbone!

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.600
We just need to win next time.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.810
Can we?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:16.990
In Kiso, fellow Genji Lord Yoshinaka
is steadily gaining power.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.450
You're the clan head. Don't be outdone.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.880
Yoshinaka.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.090
Huh?

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.300
Hey!

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.480
Yoritomo lost?!

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.400
Well, it seems the Heike didn't pursue
much, so it wasn't a total rout.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.990
I'll fight the Heike too!

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.320
Hey, Kanehira, whad'ya think?

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.410
Knowing you, I believe you will.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:11.790
Yoritomo and Yoshinaka. I'll show the
world that the Genji have two generals!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.290
Well said!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:18.090
When your father and Yoritomo's fought,

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:24.680
you were but a babe. I took you
in my arms and fled to Kiso.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.720
I never dreamed we would
defeat the Heike together!

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.930
Truly.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.140
I, Tomoe, shall fight alongside you!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.650
Things have gotten exciting,
huh, Yoshinaka!

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.020
Sure have!

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.150
Thanks to Shigehira
and Koremori's efforts,

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.280
Yoritomo lost the battle at Sunomatagawa.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.910
However, Yoshinaka subjugated Shinano
and is attempting to take Hokuriku next.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:54.250
Brother, you must act quickly!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:56.880
Me?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:02.340
With Father gone, you are the head
of the Heike in both name and reality!

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.260
I'll make my way to Hokuriku with troops.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.220
Shigehira, what do you think?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:16.730
Koremori is correct, but I would wait
and observe for the time being.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:20.900
Yes. And the governor of Echigo
was supposed to kill Yoshinaka,

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.190
but then he suddenly died.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:31.370
I'm afraid the governor of Echigo,
Jo Sukenaga, has passed away.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:35.290
On his way to attack Yoshinaka,
a voice was heard in the sky.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:41.300
It said, "Apprehend him who allies with
the Heike, burners of the great Buddha."

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:46.470
Then he suddenly fell from his horse.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:50.430
An important man from
the so-called Echigo Taira.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.930
Among his concubines,

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:58.190
there should have been a former
<i>shirabyoshi </i>with an eye like mine.

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:01.400
Oh, perhaps you mean Lady Asagi?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.070
I heard she had lived in the capital.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.950
Could I meet her?

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:12.990
I heard that after Lord Sukenaga passed,
she left Echigo to return to the capital.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.370
No way...

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.710
After I came all the way to Echigo...

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:30.680
Come on! Drink, everyone! Drink!

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.320
Koremori.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:47.280
The warriors of Etchu, Kaga, and Echizen

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:52.370
are hastening to Kiso no Yoshinaka's
side one after the other.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:57.460
And yet our clan head Lord Munemori
sits here in revelry!

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:02.340
At this rate, Yoshinaka will march on
the capital before Yoritomo does!

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.260
We must absolutely prevent that!

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.510
A "winding stream party?"

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:14.640
Lord Munemori is throwing one.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:19.940
Apparently, you have to compose a poem
before the sake dish floats past you.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.770
So Lord Atsumori and I are trying it.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.740
But at this moment,

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:32.620
Lord Koremori is leading troops
to battle against Kiso no Yoshinaka.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:37.290
With his exploits lately, it's like
Brother is a different person.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:40.710
Word is he took Hiuchi castle in Echizen.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:44.090
I wish I could have participated too.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.760
The winding stream party
seems more fun to me.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.050
Stare.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.300
What?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:55.140
Brother is about face
the final battle with Yoshinaka.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:59.770
I'd just rather use my head
than my strength.

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:02.480
You do not seem to be using it.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.520
What was that?

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.440
Stop, you two!

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.320
Let's pray for Lord Koremori's success.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.070
We have 100,000. They have 50,000.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:14.490
With the way Brother is now,
there is nothing to fear!

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:43.480
Hear me! I am Kiso no Yoshinaka,
of the Minamoto bloodline!

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:49.320
Hear m--

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:59.040
Hear me! I am Koremori,
son of Taira no Shigemori!

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:02.870
I'm headed for ya tomorrow! Wait for me!

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:19.510
I had heard Yoshinaka was an unrefined
man, but he is surprisingly courteous.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:24.520
I guess even the monkey of Kiso
observes some ceremony.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:30.480
This is the man who took over Hokuriku.
Do not underestimate him.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.490
We will advance our forces
as soon as dawn breaks.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.990
We are not well acquainted
with these mountains.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:44.620
Our large army would fight
best on open, level ground.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.580
Lord Koremori is exactly right.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:50.710
Then let's rest up for tomorrow.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.240
Th-This is...

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.250
Surprise attack!

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.960
Prepare for battle!

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:28.960
Make haste!

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.920
Hurry! Get ready!

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.260
That sure went well.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:39.680
How brilliant to move
10,000 riders to their flank!

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:44.770
Those well-mannered fools
would never think of this tactic.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.270
Now we drive them into the valley.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.480
Let's go!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:08.710
♪ The Heike turned around to see ♪

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:12.130
♪ white banners, like floating clouds. ♪

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:19.840
♪ From in front and behind,
the enemy closed in. ♪

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.950
♪ Soldier and steed ♪

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.830
♪ plunged down and piled up,
plunged and piled, ♪

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:56.340
♪ One dreadfully deep valley,
filled in with 70,000 Heike! ♪

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:00.760
♪ The rocks sprang with blood, ♪

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:04.010
♪ and the corpses formed mounds. ♪

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:16.150
<i>Seventy thousand </i>soldiers
fell into the valley?!

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:18.400
What does that mean?

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.780
Now what happens?!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.370
Yoshinaka will march into the capital.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.080
That was...

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.960
That was hell!

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:34.670
Hurry! Yoshinaka is coming!

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:35.670
Move it!

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.840
Leave the capital?

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.510
Take the emperor,

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:43.300
and the Three Sacred Treasures as well!

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:49.980
It appears Enryakuji
will side with the Genji,

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:54.190
So we... lack sufficient forces
to oppose Yoshinaka.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:14:00.030
Oh, but there are many
Heike allies in the west!

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:04.320
It seems best to regroup
and then face Yoshinaka.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:08.200
Emperor, let's get ready for an outing.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.620
An outing where?

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.160
We will start with Fukuhara.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:16.790
Perhaps you do not remember,
but you have been there before.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.040
I decline.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.630
My, but trips are such fun.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:25.510
Then shall your mother
and I go without you?

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:32.600
I will go. Prepare at once!

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.230
Pack only essential items.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:14:59.590
Sukemori.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:03.470
You were still seeing Lady Iko?

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:04.760
Yes.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:08.050
Lady Iko chooses to remain in the capital.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:12.890
I hear many others are leaving behind
wives or children.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:16.060
Even though the city will soon
be the Genji's capital.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.520
No.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:20.190
The capital is where the emperor is.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.110
It does not have to be here.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:31.660
If the emperor and I can live
there in peace and tranquility,

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:32.950
any place is enough.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.340
And the emperor?

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:44.130
He departed safely.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:47.840
I hear Emperor Go-Shirakawa
was not seen with them.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:51.930
It would appear he snuck out
of his estate last night.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.600
Go to Fukuhara with the Heike?!

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.060
Give me refuge here in Kurama.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.610
We aren't fighting Yoshinaka?

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:07.700
Even if we repelled Yoshinaka,
the monks of Mt. Hiei would attack.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.490
Yoritomo might come as well.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:14.080
If we fight together, we can
defeat the likes of the Genji!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:19.000
Is Koremori still not here?
We have to leave now.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:22.750
Father,

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.300
you will come back for us soon, right?

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.220
We'll be waiting for you.

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:32.510
Brother.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:39.350
Please make haste. The others have left.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.020
Sorry.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:48.400
If I hadn't lost so many
warriors at Kurikara Pass...

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.160
This is all my fault!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.530
I cannot face the clan.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:57.000
I have no right to leave with them!

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.830
It's not your fault, Brother!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:04.670
Besides, we will raise
another army in the west.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.840
We aren't just leaving the capital!

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.300
Kiyotsune.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.510
I'm sorry.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:14.430
I'm sorry!

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.480
Light it up!

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:24.060
Surely we don't need to burn it.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:27.480
As if I would just let the Genji have it!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:32.530
By the time they enter the capital,
50,000 estates will be reduced to ash!

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.500
This is awful.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:54.550
I didn't expect Lord Kiyomori's precious
Fukuhara to be this run down.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:57.140
It's near the ocean,
and the wind is strong.

00:17:57.140 --> 00:18:00.890
What's more, it's been
abandoned for three years.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:05.650
We'll stay here tonight,
and tomorrow we'll sail to Dazaifu.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.190
Dazaifu...

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:12.070
I suppose even Yoshinaka would
not come after us that far away.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:16.990
Emperor, this is your first time staying
somewhere like this, isn't it?

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.580
Will there not be ghosts?

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:22.960
If there are, I, Tomomori,
shall apprehend them!

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:25.920
I hope you will grant
me your aid, Emperor.

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:27.460
Very well!

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.960
That's the spirit!

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:35.550
Lord Kiyotsune.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.970
Lord Atsumori.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:41.560
I thought I might find you here.

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.150
Come to think of it, we played here.

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:52.490
Yes, along with Lord Shigehira.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.910
It feels like an eternity ago.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:59.330
Lord Kiyotsune...

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:06.210
Before we left the capital,
Koremori was crying and blaming himself.

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.290
As if this were all his fault.

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:17.890
Our clan was driven from the capital
and has to stay in this desolate place.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:20.390
Why is this happening to us?

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:24.060
Lord Kiyotsune,
please pull yourself together.

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.600
Now <i>we </i>will join the fight!

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:31.690
Our 100,000 troops now number only 7,000.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:35.360
How can we fight Yoshinaka or Yoritomo?

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.860
I choose to fight!

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:42.910
Isn't that how Lord Kiyomori and
his father climbed to the top?

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.960
Let's take your mind off it.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:50.880
Not tonight, Lord Atsumori.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:56.630
The sound of a flute in this
desolation would be too sad.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:15.860
So the place Father staked
his dreams on is to be ash, too.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:20.820
The Heike has allies in the west!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.740
To Dazaifu!

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.720
To think we'd see white Genji
banners in the capital.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:45.970
It's been, what, 20 years?

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.600
Please, give that back!

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.520
Shut up!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.570
I'll teach you to behave!

00:20:57.240 --> 00:20:58.400
Mercy!

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:59.530
Please let me go!

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:01.110
Come on. Go inside!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:04.160
What's this?

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:06.290
Get off!

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.420
Time to run!

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.260
My biwa! My cat!

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:19.930
Don't worry!

00:21:21.010 --> 00:21:22.140
Stop!

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:24.600
Hey, just drop it.

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:25.640
Dammit.
